{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/835188-2ed-explain-to-me-contracts","id":835188,"title":"[2ED] Explain to me Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-22T11:07:11-08:00","id":835188,"title":"[2ED] Explain to me Contracts","content":"We got our <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832066-2e-playtest-compilation-now-with-pledges-and-huntsmen\">Playtest Files</a> and I'm making my <b>Changeling</b> 2ED character right now. I was a bit shocked when I got to the Contracts section and truly could not get straight image how they work in proposed rules system, even after over decade of playing and running the <b>CoD</b> systems. So I nicely ask you, my fellow co-forumates, to easy and enlighten me on the matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Character Creation document states on Contracts...<br /> <br /> <i>Contracts are the binding agreements made by the True Fae with reality. Fire burns in Arcadia, for example, because the owner of that particular part of Faerie contracted to burn. Changelings, as beings that are between Fae and human, can exploit clauses of these Contracts for their own benefit. Select five dots worth of Contracts from p. XX. At least two dots have to be in Contracts that feature your character\u2019s Seeming as a favored option. If you purchase a Contract with affinity for your character\u2019s Seeming, you get that affinity effect for free. You cannot start play with the affinity effects for other Seemings. </i><br /> <br /> Okay, this is simply - I only need to spend 5 dots in total on Contracts...<br /> <br /> But then I go to the Contracts document itself and I got this...<br /> <br /> <i>Each Contract has a dot rating which costs one experience per dot. Most have no prerequisites and can be bought immediately. Every Contract also has favored seemings that invoke effects in addition to the basic Contract. If a changeling is of that seeming, she gains the effect for free upon purchasing the Contract. Otherwise, she may learn the effect from a teacher and pay one<br /> experience for it. A player can purchase as many favored effects per Contract as she wishes and can activate none, any, or all of them, as long as she pays all their costs (if any) regardless of using the Catch.<br /> <br /> Seeming effects are flavored to fit that Seeming. A Contract that allows an Elemental to create lava traps in her path, lets a Wizened rapidly craft small clockwork monsters to attack pursuers. Players are encouraged to further tailor a Contract's effects to her character. When your character invokes Light-Shy, does she hear her Keeper's raspy whispers, or see her doom spelled in the f? Some Contracts have multiple dot ratings, with the higher version having greater effects. If your character has the lesser version, she can improve her Contract rating by paying the difference in experience; she doesn\u2019t have to purchase the greater version as a new Contract altogether.</i><br /> <br /> Okay, this sounds still reasonable. However, when I got to the Contract write-ups itself, I see those...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>One Dot Contracts </b></span><br /> <br /> Bite of the Wooden Fang (\u2022)<br /> Changeling Fate (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Cloak of the Elements (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Fang and Talon (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Mask of Superiority (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Two Dot Contracts </b></span><br /> <br /> Boon of the Scuttling Spider (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Changeling Hours (\u2022\u2022\u2013\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Dreamsteps (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Light\u2013Shy (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Murkblur (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Thorns and Brambles (\u2022\u2022\u2013\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> My questions are those:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>HOW I make a starting &quot;buy&quot; of Contracts?</b> Are they rated as lists &quot;One Dot Contracts&quot;, &quot;Two Dot Contracts&quot;, etc? Or I just look over (\u2022\u2022\u2013\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) dots near particular Contract and buy those?<br /> <br /> 2. <b>WHERE are my Seemings affinity options?</b> I need having two DOTS of those Contracts or two CONTRACTS itself?<br /> <br /> Thanks for understanding this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-22-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:18:44-08:00","id":835200,"title":"","content":"Contracts are costed like Merits. They're organized by the minimum dot cost, so Changeling Fate, for example, is under One-Dot Contracts because the most basic version is one dot. You can buy the second and/or third dot to gain additional effects, as described in the Contract.<br /> <br /> Seeming affinity bonuses are the last part of the Contract description. Notice how some of them say things like<br /> Beast: Do an extra thing.<br /> Fairest: Do a different extra thing.<br /> <br /> If your character is one of those Seemings, you get that additional bonus for free. If your character is a different Seeming, you can still gain those bonuses, but they cost 1 experience each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:30:09-08:00","id":835218,"title":"","content":"For character creation, I think it's also like merits: you get 5 dots to spend. You can buy a 5-dot contract, five 1-dots, two 2-dots and a 1-dot, etc. For Contracts with a range, you can buy them at whatever level, much like with ranged Merits/Fighting Styles. So I could get Bite of the Wooden Fang 1, Cloak of the Elements (Water) 3, and Fang and Talon 1, or Cloak of the Elements (Water) 1 and Thornes and Brambles 4, or whatever. The total number of dots stays 5. <br /> <br /> At character creation, I think you only get freebe Seeming benefits; it doesn't seem like you can buy them. So if there's a Seeming benefit in the Contract you buy, you have it; otherwise, you don't. Later on you can learn them with XP, but not starting. (Although I could also see getting a out-of-Seeming benefit at the cost of one of your five starting Contract dots with ST approval.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:32:58-08:00","id":835221,"title":"","content":"You start with 5 dots of contracts, two of those dots have to be in contracts that have an affinity to your seeming, weather it be one 2-dot contract, or two 1-dot contacts, or part of a contract that costs 3-5.<br /> <br /> but if you choose 1 or 2 dot contracts and then choose a non affinity contract, you don't, or cant purchase the seeming affinity of another seeming, until you're able to have it taught at a later time<br /> <br /> Quote from pdf: <b>Select five dots worth of Contracts from p. XX. At least two dots have to be in Contracts<br /> <br /> that feature your character\u2019s Seeming as a favored option. If you purchase a Contract with<br /> <br /> affinity for your character\u2019s Seeming, you get that affinity effect for free. You cannot start play<br /> <br /> with the affinity effects for other Seemings.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:34:35-08:00","id":835223,"title":"","content":"One dot contracts have one dot or more. Two dot contracts have two dots or more. And so on. They have a total number of dots, and that is what matters to calculate how you buy them, from what I can tell.<br /> <br /> I don't understand your second question, but in summary: when you buy a contract, you get the affinity effect matching your Seeming for free. If the contract has no affinity for your Seeming, you don't get any. Then you can buy any of the seeming affinities you don't have for 1 Experience each, but you buy them separately between contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-22-2016, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:37:40-08:00","id":835226,"title":"","content":"Okay I'll if I can explain it using Cloak of the Elements.<br /> <br /> Say your character is an elemental. He or She picks Cloak of Elements.<br /> <br /> Using his first 5 free dots of contracts he buys a \u2022 Cloak of Elements and \u2022 Bite of the Wooden Fang, both of which have elemental effects underneath the contract description, which your Character gets for free.<br /> <br /> The elemental effect for Cloak of the Elements is that your character can use two elements at the same time and the elementak benifit of bite of the wooden fang is your wooden weapon utilizes your element to boost its grappling bonus by +3.<br /> <br /> Now you have 3 free contact dots left and can be spent on a 3 dit contract, a 1 dot contract and a 2 dot contract or 3 one dot contracts, and they do not need to have an elemental effect because you have already meant that requirement with Cloak of the Elements and Bite of the Wooden Fang.<br /> <br /> Alternately you could have spent \u2022\u2022 on Cloak of the Elements to get a stronger verison, which would met the Seeming requirements on its own.<br /> <br /> But say you went with my original choices andas you earn experience you wish to boost Cloak of the Elements which has the option of just being a 1 dot contract or a 2 dot cobtract or a 3 dot contract.<br /> <br /> You spend 1experience point by an additional dot of Cloak of the Elements which makes the contract stronger, so your 1 dot contract, becones a 2 dot contract. Later you could spend another experience point and buy the 3rd dot in Cloak of the Elements making it more powerful and turning it into a 3 dot cobtract. But that's as high as Cloak of the Elements goes, its a 1 to 3 dot contract. <br /> <br /> Wooden Fang on the other hand is just a 1 dot contract and you can't buy extra dots in it to boost it into being a higher dot contract.<br /> <br /> What can do with you now 3 dot verison of the Cloak of the Elements is buy another seeming effect. Cloak of the Elements has a Seeming effect that is natural to elementals,which you got for free, but also one for the Fairest which as an Elemental you have to pay 1 experience point for. <br /> <br /> Say you do, now not only can use you 2 Cloaks of the Elements, your Cloak also boosts you intimidate die pools, ehich is the Fairest Effect for that contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T13:36:57-08:00","id":835329,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, <i>Cloak of Elements</i> example hit the nail most in my head. If someone have other questions on Contracts - feel free to use this topic for asking them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T19:00:14-08:00","id":835501,"title":"","content":"Your welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}